  "verbalization": "Neocomplanoside is implicated in the biological activity against T-24 through a series of molecular interactions involving the serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2. This kinase is a target of multiple compounds, including Diosmetin-7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-6-O-Acetyl-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-Lrhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, Phlegmanol C, and Yesanchinoside J. All these compounds share a common target, CDC2L2, which is a key regulator of the cell cycle and has been shown to be a potential therapeutic target in various cancers. The evidence suggests that Neocomplanoside may exert its biological effects by modulating the activity of CDC2L2, which in turn influences the behavior of T-24 cells. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Neocomplanoside to act as a modulator of CDC2L2, thereby affecting T-24 cell function. The relationship is supported by the shared target and the presence of multiple compounds with similar mechanisms, reinforcing the likelihood of a direct or indirect interaction between Neocomplanoside and T-24 through the CDC2L2 pathway.",
